<title>USA: VideoLabs president and CEO retires.</title>
<headline>VideoLabs president and CEO retires.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>VideoLabs Inc said Thursday president and chief executive officer Ward Johnson has retired.</p>
<p>He was replaced, as of Thursday, by James Hansen, a business advisor, the video products company said. Johnson, who had been president since 1992, will remain chairman of the board, the company said.</p>
<p>VideoLab shares were unchanged at 1-5/8.</p>
<p>Earlier Thursday, the company reported net income of $7.1 million, $0.00 a share in the third quarter, compared to $235.1 million, or $0.08 a share a year ago.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
